module test.claim.import_admission_closure_membership_witness_test


data import_admission_closure_membership_note: String = "THE IMPORT LIST DOES NOT GATE A BARE FREE CALL; CLOSURE MEMBERSHIP DOES. Four arms, one instrument, one binary, differing only in how the probe reaches the provider module. MEASURED on main (dag/test/fixture/import_admission_provider declares import_admission_listed and import_admission_unlisted): (1) LISTED -- the probe selectively imports the provider AND names import_admission_unlisted -- resolves, zero blocking rows, and this is the only arm whose green is CORRECT. (2) SELECTIVE-UNLISTED -- the probe selectively imports the provider and does NOT name import_admission_unlisted -- ALSO resolves, zero blocking rows. The author wrote the admitted surface of that module and the compiler served a name outside it. (3) POOL-COINCIDENCE -- the probe never imports the provider at all, only a carrier that does -- ALSO resolves, zero blocking rows. Nothing in this probe's own text mentions the provider. (4) ABSENT-FROM-CLOSURE -- nothing reaches the provider -- REFUSES, one blocking row, function 'import_admission_unlisted' not found in scope. Arm (4) is the discriminating control and it is what makes arms (1) to (3) readable: the instrument CAN go red on this exact proposition, so three greens are three measurements and not three vacuous passes. Read together the four cells say one thing: what admits a bare free call is whether the declaring module is in the compiled closure, and the import statement's name list contributes nothing to that decision -- it only influences the closure. THE TWO DEFECT ARMS ARE PINNED, NOT ASSERTED AS CORRECT. Arms (2) and (3) assert what the compiler does today so the class stays visible and any change to it is loud; when the admission wall lands they must FLIP to blocking, and a flip is the wall landing rather than this witness breaking. WHY NOT A WALL IN THIS PULL REQUEST, stated because the obvious repair was built and measured and withdrawn. Two placements were implemented and executed against the v1 self-host closure. Placing the refusal at the whole-pool census seams (borrowed_census_decl, global_bare_callable_node) is a DECORATION: the closure regenerated to a byte-identical fixed point, 134 of 134 planned, first_generation_equal=true, and arm (2) still did not fire -- because a selectively-imported module's unlisted fn is served EARLIER, by the unfiltered parent func_env and by the ancestry_str_bindings overlay, so the census fallback the brief names is never reached and there is no parent miss to fall through from. gunbc#9075's parent-env filter, applied on top and measured, does not create that miss either; the ancestry overlay still serves the name. Placing the refusal at the admission seam itself (lookup_func_sig) does bite -- the same closure went from a clean fixed point to three hard diagnostics -- but it bites by returning an unresolved signature, which degrades downstream into 'if branches resolve to incompatible types: Primitive(cost_constant) vs Primitive(CostBound)', a diagnostic that names neither the unadmitted call nor the import that declined it. That is a silent widen wearing a type error, not the typed located refusal DESIGN section 5 requires. So the machinery was deleted rather than shipped unproven, and the measurement is what lands. THE EXISTING AUTHORITY FOR THIS CLASS IS UnlistedImportUse, and it already covers the TYPE positions only: 04_resolve.dag's resolve_node emits it advisory when masked and the name is outside source_visible_names, with resolve_node_bounded_masked_boundary declaring the promotion to a hard refusal once the corpus burndown reaches zero. The value/call position emits NOTHING, which is why this half of the class has no count. Extending that same diagnostic to the call seam -- same predicate, same advisory posture, same burndown -- is the next increment, and it is one authority extended rather than a second wall minted beside it. SIZING, and its provenance is stated because the two halves were measured differently. The selective-unlisted half is 186 call sites across 118 modules over dag, src/v2 and src/v1, from a static join of module declarations, import lists and fn declarations -- a static estimate, not a compiler measurement, and it is an upper bound because it cannot see local binders that shadow a name. The pool-coincidence half has no trustworthy static number: the same join reports 4784 sites, but arm (4) shows the census only serves what the closure loads, so that figure counts sites whose provider may never be in any real closure. It is recorded here as an unbounded class rather than a count. RUNG (DESIGN section 4b): outside the ladder -- silent wrongness. A bare call's meaning depends on which modules the closure happened to load, and no diagnostic reports it at the value position. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- admission is decidable from the consumer's own resolved_imports joined to the census candidate's owner module, both already carried. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: UnlistedImportUse extended to the call seam, which makes the population countable and is the precondition resolve_node_bounded_masked_boundary already names for promoting the advisory to a wall. THE HARD-CODED name == 'trim' IN bare_free_call_requires_listed_import IS THE ONE NAME FOR WHICH THE IMPORT LIST IS LOAD-BEARING, and it is a hand patch of arm (3), not of arm (2). It is untouched here; its own dissolve-on, the PrimitiveDefinition identity-join in closure_independent_bare_free_call_note, is unchanged and is not a rule this pull request can derive. dissolve-on: never -- arms (1) and (4) are permanent regression controls for the admission law, and arms (2) and (3) become permanent regression controls the moment they flip."

data import_admission_listed_source: String = "module import_admission_green_probe\n\nimport std.types \{ Int \}\nimport test.fixture.import_admission_provider \{ import_admission_listed, import_admission_unlisted \}\n\nfn probe(value: Int) -> Int \{ import_admission_unlisted(import_admission_listed(value)) \}\n"

data import_admission_selective_unlisted_source: String = "module import_admission_selective_unlisted_probe\n\nimport std.types \{ Int \}\nimport test.fixture.import_admission_provider \{ import_admission_listed \}\n\nfn probe(value: Int) -> Int \{ import_admission_unlisted(import_admission_listed(value)) \}\n"

data import_admission_pool_coincidence_source: String = "module import_admission_pool_coincidence_probe\n\nimport std.types \{ Int \}\nimport test.fixture.import_admission_pool_carrier \{ import_admission_carrier \}\n\nfn probe(value: Int) -> Int \{ import_admission_unlisted(import_admission_carrier(value)) \}\n"

data import_admission_absent_from_closure_source: String = "module import_admission_absent_from_closure_probe\n\nimport std.types \{ Int \}\n\nfn probe(value: Int) -> Int \{ import_admission_unlisted(value) \}\n"

fn import_admission_blocking_row_count(source: String) -> Int {
  match compile_dag_diagnostic_census(source) {
    gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census.CensusObserved { rows: rows } => count(gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census.census_blocking_rows(rows: rows))
    gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census.CensusNotRunnable { cause: _ } => 0 - 1
  }
}

test fn listed_name_resolves() -> Bool {
  import_admission_blocking_row_count(source: import_admission_listed_source) == 0
}

test fn selective_unlisted_name_still_resolves_today() -> Bool {
  import_admission_blocking_row_count(source: import_admission_selective_unlisted_source) == 0
}

test fn pool_coincidence_name_still_resolves_today() -> Bool {
  import_admission_blocking_row_count(source: import_admission_pool_coincidence_source) == 0
}

test fn name_absent_from_the_closure_refuses() -> Bool {
  import_admission_blocking_row_count(source: import_admission_absent_from_closure_source) > 0
}
